# Frontend

Stack: React, Vite, TypeScript in `apps/frontend`.

## Structure

- `components/` — shared UI only (Button, Card, Modal, VideoPlayer, Accordion)
- `features/<domain>/` — courses, lessons, activities, admin
- `layouts/` — `PublicLayout`, `AdminLayout`
- `pages/` — public pages plus `/admin` pages
- `hooks/` — reusable hooks
- `lib/` — API client and admin token handling

## Data and auth

- All HTTP calls go through the API client in `src/lib`, using `VITE_API_BASE_URL`.
- Admin JWT read/write lives only in `src/lib`. Components never touch the token directly.
- Routes under `/admin` use `AdminLayout` and are guarded by the token check.
- Quiz feedback comes only from `POST /api/activities/:id/check`. `GET /api/activities/:id` has no answers.
- Never persist learner answers, scores, or progress. Do not use `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` for them.

## Pages

- Implement each page exactly as the supplied layout. Do not invent or restyle layouts.
- Every data view has loading, empty, and error states.

```tsx
// Bad: fetch inside a component
const res = await fetch(`${import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL}/api/courses`);

// Good: use the shared client
const courses = await api.get<Course[]>("/api/courses");
```
